  (global_label "GND" (shape bidirectional) (at 87.63 184.15 270) (fields_autoplaced yes) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify right)) (uuid "019e5749-cf7f-4412-a217-0ed02ba10c61"))
  (text "RPi Camera LED interposer: sits between a Raspberry Pi and its camera.\nMIPI lanes, I2C, GND and 3V3 pass straight through J1 -> J2.\nU1 (I2C slave on the camera bus) drives the camera GPIO pins 11/12,\nPWM-drives the illumination LEDs and reads ambient light on its ADC." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 20 30 0) (effects (font (size 2.0 2.0)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "529f647c-7775-4613-83f1-c4edccbc8bc1"))
  (text "Fit R6/R7 (0R) to pass the Pi's own CAM_IO pins through\nwhen U1 is not populated. I2C and the Qwiic header work regardless." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 108 164 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "54c640d3-cec4-4850-9ffa-9371515cf8ba"))
  (text "Pin 8 = PD1/SWIO (bonded with PD4/PD5): programming and LED gate share\nit; LEDs flicker while flashing firmware. PD1/T1CH3N gives hardware PWM." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 95 193 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "9615e711-c93a-448a-8ea5-6a20b7bb5fe5"))
  (text "LED current is set by R3/R4 against the 3V3 rail (about 30-40mA each\nwith Vf=2.9V). Total draw comes from the Pi camera 3V3 supply - keep\nthe duty/current within the Pi's camera connector budget." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 183 32 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "8e065616-7869-4380-83c4-c473fc4f7b2a"))
  (text "All parts chosen for JLCPCB / NextPCB Rev0 assembly; see\nresearch/*.md for availability and pricing (checked 2026-09-01)." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 20 195 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "16e00c74-a065-48ce-8122-8d16fa096013"))
